Map frontends
  output/*/data.min.json follows the data shape of the map frontend from
  https://github.com/mxmap/mxmap-ch (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 David Huser), which
  is also the basis of sslmap.nbrt.ch. No frontend code is included here.

Web map (web/)
  Leaflet 1.9.4 (BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2010-2023 Vladimir Agafonkin,
  (c) 2010-2011 CloudMade), stylesheet copied to web/vendor/leaflet.css;
  script loaded from unpkg.com. topojson-client 3.1.0 (ISC), loaded from unpkg.com.
  Boundaries: swiss-maps 4.7.0 (interactivethings), based on swisstopo data.

Inspiration
  sslmap.nbrt.ch, map of Swiss public-sector TLS certificates (2026).

Data sources used at run time
  Common CA Database (CCADB), https://www.ccadb.org, CA owner per issuing CA.
  Certificate Transparency via Cert Spotter (SSLMate) and crt.sh (Sectigo).
  DNS via Google Public DNS and Cloudflare DNS-over-HTTPS.
  IP-to-ASN mapping via Team Cymru.

Libraries
  cryptography (Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause), openpyxl (MIT).

data/critical_services/
  Operator names, UIDs and legal seats from the UID register of the Swiss
  Federal Statistical Office (BFS), queried through its public web service
  https://www.uid-wse.admin.ch/V5.0/PublicServices.svc in November 2026.
  Sector and sub-sector names from the Nationale Strategie zum Schutz
  kritischer Infrastrukturen of 16 June 2023 (BBl 2023 1659) and
  https://www.babs.admin.ch/de/die-kritischen-infrastrukturen.
